hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"28171","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid ibn Jubayr ibn Shaybah, on the authority of Said ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Umm Sharik, on the authority of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He ordered her to kill geckos."
"28172","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah say: Umm Sharik informed me that she heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: People will flee from the Dajjal into the mountains. Umm Sharik said: O Messenger of Allah, where will the Arabs be on that day? He said: All of them few."
"28173","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Umm Sharik, that she was among those who offered themselves to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
